OL,3,ACrossCountry train services resume
OL,4,Aafter outage
OL,5,
OL,6,FTrain operator CrossCountry says it
OL,7,Fexpects to run a full service on Monday
OL,8,Fafter cancelling nearly all of its UK
OL,9,Fservices the day before following a
OL,10,Fpower cut at its control centre.
OL,12,FThe outage in Birmingham at the weekend
OL,13,Fbrought disruption from Glasgow to
OL,14,FPenzance.
OL,16,FMajor routes were affected between
OL,17,FBirmingham and Manchester, which pass
OL,18,Fthrough Stoke-on-Trent, Coventry and
OL,19,FWolverhampton. Journeys from Leeds to
OL,20,FYork and Cheltenham to Cardiff were
OL,21,Falso caught in the travel chaos,
OL,22,Fleaving passengers frustrated.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,0,100
